<title>JAPAN: Nissan shares rise on cost-cutting plans.</title>
<headline>Nissan shares rise on cost-cutting plans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nissan Motor Co Ltd shares crawled higher in Tuesday afternoon trade as investors welcomed the carmaker's plans to cut costs, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0600 GMT, the shares were up 10 yen at 817 yen.</p>
<p>Nissan said on Tuesday it plans to drastically reduce the types of car platforms it uses by the year 2000 in order to cut production and development costs.</p>
</text>
